Subject: Python.h before the C++ standard headers (python_utils.h, python_object_wrapper.h, main.cc)
Error: /usr/include/python3.11/pyconfig.h:1793:9: error: '_POSIX_C_SOURCE' redefined [-Werror]
  /usr/include/features.h:319:10: note: this is the location of the previous definition (202405L)
  /usr/include/python3.11/pyconfig.h:1817:9: error: '_XOPEN_SOURCE' redefined [-Werror]
Why: <type_traits> (included first) pulls in glibc's features.h, which with _GNU_SOURCE defines the POSIX.1-2024
  values (glibc 2.44: 202405L / 800); pyconfig.h then redefines them to 200809L / 700 and the shell builds with
  -Werror. Every Wolfi Python (3.11-3.14) has the same pyconfig.h values, so no Python choice avoids it. Python's
  documented rule is to include Python.h before any standard header; then features.h replaces the values with an
  #undef and nothing warns. Percona's el9/Debian builds use older glibc, where the values are equal.
Upstream: none found (searched mysql/mysql-shell at tag 9.7.1)
Drop-when: mysql-shell includes Python.h first upstream, or pyconfig.h and glibc agree again
